WEBVTT

00:00:03.141 --> 00:00:05.361
Let's go over some external
components,

00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:06.560
jams and supplies.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.041
So I'm going to open up each
compartment where jams

00:00:10.061 --> 00:00:11.061
might occur.

00:00:11.921 --> 00:00:16.320
Anything green or blue inside the
machine is safe

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.560
to touch or maneuver, and they're
all labeled.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.261
So the FS2 means finisher,

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:22.860
component two,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.960
and anything blue means supplies or
sensors.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.981
So this is your hole punch you'll
empty out when it's

00:00:30.001 --> 00:00:31.001
full.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.420
If you have that component, when
this is empty,

00:00:34.441 --> 00:00:36.401
this will move forward, and you're
replacing this

00:00:36.421 --> 00:00:39.541
clear cartridge here in this blue
piece here.

00:00:39.561 --> 00:00:43.920
And there's a picture illustration
here to help guide

00:00:43.941 --> 00:00:45.120
you through that.

00:00:47.741 --> 00:00:50.761
You have an external stapler here
with this finisher

00:00:50.781 --> 00:00:52.181
up to 50 sheets.

00:00:52.221 --> 00:00:53.441
Print or copy.

00:00:54.261 --> 00:00:56.821
So anything you want stapled,

00:00:57.741 --> 00:00:58.861
just insert.

00:01:00.541 --> 00:01:01.973
Again, up to 50 sheets.

00:01:01.993 --> 00:01:04.253
Not very much green in here.

00:01:04.273 --> 00:01:07.833
There's three green, M2, M1, and M3,

00:01:07.853 --> 00:01:10.213
but generally in here you see the
paper sticking out.

00:01:10.433 --> 00:01:12.253
It's really hot in here, so be
careful,

00:01:12.273 --> 00:01:14.693
but I recommend pulling it out with
two hands so nothing

00:01:14.713 --> 00:01:17.193
rips off and causes further issues
where you might

00:01:17.213 --> 00:01:19.393
need a tech. And with this door,

00:01:19.673 --> 00:01:21.593
you kind of have to use some force
when closing it.

00:01:21.613 --> 00:01:24.233
And here, sometimes people forget to
remove their

00:01:24.253 --> 00:01:29.413
staples or their paper clips, and
this is a part you

00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:30.213
might have to open here.

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:31.493
This is DF1.

00:01:31.813 --> 00:01:33.333
But again, just a reminder,

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:35.493
you'll see

00:01:37.313 --> 00:01:39.953
some guided instructions, very
detailed.

00:01:40.513 --> 00:01:42.193
So it shows that I've opened that
component,

00:01:42.213 --> 00:01:44.413
but you'll also see some text
guiding you.

00:01:44.433 --> 00:01:48.153
Again, it might say open DF1, turn
FS5,

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:49.553
turn FS1.

00:01:49.933 --> 00:01:53.493
And this little hand here indicates
you have to close

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.960
it correctly by pushing there.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.740
And your ADF, this is a sensor also,

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.660
holds up to 300 sheets.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.580
And just more on the sensors.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.420
If I load this and this sensor gets
maneuvered,

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.440
moved,

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.060
it's beeping at me.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.320
Why are you beeping at me?

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.920
I can look at that message center.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:15.640
It says paper is not, there's no
matching paper size

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.660
of A4.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.280
But as soon as I adjust the sensor
back to eight and

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.587
a half by eleven, that message goes
away.

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.587
And there's your toner.

00:02:23.847 --> 00:02:25.507
This pops out.

00:02:25.827 --> 00:02:28.667
Out of box, pull off any orange tape
and insert the

00:02:28.687 --> 00:02:29.195
toner.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.855
Your waste toner box.

00:02:30.995 --> 00:02:31.995
There's that blue.

00:02:32.455 --> 00:02:34.075
This whole unit gets replaced.

00:02:34.335 --> 00:02:36.715
When this is full, the machine is
non-operable.

00:02:37.155 --> 00:02:39.035
So when you see this orange light
blinking,

00:02:39.215 --> 00:02:40.456
look on that message center.

00:02:40.476 --> 00:02:42.216
Right now it says it's warming up,

00:02:42.236 --> 00:02:44.396
but you'll see this blinking.

00:02:44.416 --> 00:02:46.576
It will say replace waste toner box
soon.

00:02:46.816 --> 00:02:48.796
So these sensors are very important.

00:02:48.956 --> 00:02:51.956
Always make sure they're adjusted to
the paper size in the

00:02:51.976 --> 00:02:52.976
tray.

00:02:53.036 --> 00:02:55.436
Let's say it gets maneuvered just a
little bit.

00:02:55.456 --> 00:02:57.556
Someone's loading more paper or just
accidentally

00:02:57.576 --> 00:02:58.616
gets maneuvered.

00:02:59.636 --> 00:03:01.876
You never want to see question
marks.

00:03:01.896 --> 00:03:04.896
So right now it's showing tray 1
question marks because

00:03:04.916 --> 00:03:06.836
it's not detecting that size.

00:03:07.936 --> 00:03:09.376
But as soon as I adjust,

00:03:11.136 --> 00:03:13.456
the question marks go away and it
knows what tray

00:03:13.476 --> 00:03:16.116
to pull from. So now when I'm
sending print or copy

00:03:16.136 --> 00:03:19.096
jobs, it knows tray 1 has 8.5 x 11
and I'm going to

00:03:19.116 --> 00:03:20.176
pull from that tray.

00:03:20.636 --> 00:03:23.196
If you see these light up orange,

00:03:23.216 --> 00:03:24.876
it means that tray is out of paper.

00:03:24.921 --> 00:03:27.681
You have your flash drive option
here on the right

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:32.141
side. You can print and save to User
Box with your USB

00:03:32.161 --> 00:03:32.576
drive.

00:03:32.596 --> 00:03:34.556
Anything you scan on the glass,

00:03:34.576 --> 00:03:36.396
make sure it's top left corner.

00:03:36.796 --> 00:03:38.896
You see here there's a ruler so it
goes by paper size

00:03:38.916 --> 00:03:41.285
and top left corner is 8.5 x 11
start.

00:03:41.305 --> 00:03:44.585
To order supplies or place a service
call,

00:03:44.605 --> 00:03:47.885
call this 800 number and have this
eight-digit ID handy.

00:03:48.325 --> 00:03:51.785
Or if you have the newer KM sticker,

00:03:51.805 --> 00:03:55.385
you have a QR code here which you
can use with your

00:03:55.405 --> 00:03:58.885
phone to bring up the app to place a
service call

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.504
for service or supplies.

00:04:00.524 --> 00:04:02.904
So thank you. I hope that helped.

00:04:03.864 --> 00:04:06.044
I'm creating videos in increments,

00:04:06.064 --> 00:04:07.204
so that was external.

00:04:07.224 --> 00:04:09.544
I'll do one on copying and I'll do
one on scanning.

00:04:09.744 --> 00:04:12.364
And I hope it helps you until I can
get on site.
